#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:2
msgid "Quick Start Evaluation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:4
msgid ""
"This guide provides instructions for quickly trying out Mattermost using "
"either Docker or Azure Marketplace. These options are ideal for testing "
"and evaluation purposes as they allow you to quickly get a Mattermost "
"instance up and running for exploration and testing. However, these quick"
" start options are not recommended for production use. They are "
"configured for demonstration purposes only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:7
msgid "Deployment options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:12
msgid ""
"Mattermost is published as an **Azure Marketplace** solution that deploys"
" a single Ubuntu virtual machine with Mattermost, PostgreSQL, network "
"configurations, and the necessary Azure resources. This quick start "
"evaluation option is preferred for customers already using Azure, as it "
"integrates seamlessly within their existing infrastructure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:15
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:17
msgid ""
"An active **Azure subscription** with permission to create resources and "
"accept **Azure Marketplace** billing terms for the offer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:18
msgid ""
"Familiarity with the **Azure portal** (resource groups, networking, and "
"virtual machines)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:21
msgid "What gets deployed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:23
msgid ""
"The template provisions a small, self-contained stack in the resource "
"group you select, including:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:25
msgid ""
"**Virtual machine (Linux):** Runs Mattermost, PostgreSQL, and the reverse"
" proxy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:26
msgid ""
"**Public IP address:** Allows access to the Mattermost workspace over the"
" public internet, enabling users to connect to the platform securely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:27
msgid ""
"**Network interface:** Facilitates communication between the Virtual "
"Machine and other Azure resources through a defined network layer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:28
msgid ""
"**Network security group:** Acts as a virtual firewall, controlling "
"inbound and outbound traffic to protect the deployed resources from "
"unauthorized access."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:29
msgid ""
"**Managed OS disk:** Provides persistent storage mounted to the Virtual "
"Machine for storing files generated by Mattermost, including uploaded "
"documents and system configurations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:30
msgid ""
"**Virtual network:** An isolated network environment for the deployed "
"resources, enabling private and controlled connectivity between "
"infrastructure components. This can be a newly created or existing "
"environment depending on your selection in the portal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:34
msgid "Step 1: Select a plan and start creation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:36
msgid ""
"Go to the `Mattermost - Quick Start Evaluation (VM) "
"<https://azuremarketplace.microsoft.com/en-us/marketplace/apps/mattermost"
".mattermost-all-in-one>`_ Azure Marketplace application to begin. Click "
"**Get it now**, then select the **Mattermost - Quick Start Evaluation "
"(VM)** plan, and click **Create** to open the deployment wizard."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:40
msgid "Step 2: Basic Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:42
msgid "On the **Basics** tab, configure the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:44
msgid ""
"**Subscription:** Choose the Azure subscription where the deployment will"
" live."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:45
msgid ""
"**Resource group:** Either select an existing resource group or create a "
"new one. Using a **new** resource group keeps evaluation resources easy "
"to find."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:46
msgid ""
"**Region:** Select the deployment region for your Virtual Machine (for "
"example, **East US** or **West Europe**)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:47
msgid "**Virtual Machine name:** Provide a unique name for your Virtual Machine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:48
msgid "**Username:** Linux administrator account on the VM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:49
msgid ""
"**Email:** Used for Let's Encrypt registration when the instance requests"
" a TLS certificate. Use a mailbox you can access since you may receive "
"operational emails from the certificate authority."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:50
msgid ""
"**Support email:** Contact email for end users to reach the instance "
"administrator for troubleshooting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:51
msgid ""
"**Authentication type:** **Password** or **SSH public key** only for "
"Linux sign-in to the VM. Password is often simpler for a quick trial; SSH"
" key is appropriate if your organization requires key-based Linux access."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:54
msgid "Step 3: Virtual Machine Settings and Network Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:56
msgid "On **Virtual Machine Settings** tab, configure the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:58
msgid ""
"**Virtual machine size:** For trials, we recommend **Standard_F2s_v2** "
"size but you can choose any other size available in your region."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:59
msgid ""
"**Public IP address:** Typically **create new**. You must set a **DNS "
"prefix** (label) that is **globally unique** in Azure; it forms part of "
"your URL. This DNS will allow public access to your workspace. It is "
"important that you do not already have a matching DNS name within your "
"Azure subscription, or your deployment may fail later in the process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:60
msgid ""
"**Virtual network:** **Create new** with the suggested address space, or "
"attach an existing VNet and subnet that meet the constraints. Using a new"
" virtual network avoids collisions with overlapping address spaces in the"
" same subscription."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:62
msgid ""
"The portal may show a preview of your URL in the form ``https://<dns-"
"label>.<region>.cloudapp.azure.com``. That is the address you will use "
"once TLS and Mattermost are ready."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:65
msgid "Step 4: Review and create"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:67
msgid ""
"Review settings, accept any **Marketplace** terms if prompted, then "
"select **Create**. Provisioning usually takes a few minutes, and the "
"first-boot configuration may take more time before HTTPS works reliably."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:69
msgid "**After deployment completes:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:71
msgid "In the Azure portal, open the **resource group** you used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:72
msgid ""
"Open the **Public IP address** resource (often named ``<your-vm-"
"name>-ip`` unless you changed it)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:73
msgid "Under **Essentials**, note the **DNS name**. Your site URL is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:75
msgid "``https://<dns-label>.<region>.cloudapp.azure.com``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:77
msgid "Example: ``https://myorg.eastus.cloudapp.azure.com``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:79
msgid "Use **https**; the deployment is intended to serve Mattermost over TLS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:82
msgid "Step 5: Open Mattermost and create your administrator"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:84
msgid ""
"In a browser, go to your **HTTPS** URL. Mattermost will prompt you to "
"**create the first user**, which becomes the **System Administrator**. "
"That account is different from the **Linux** username and password (or "
"SSH key) you configured in Step 3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:86
msgid "Congratulations! You’ve successfully deployed Mattermost for evaluation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/quick-start-evaluation.rst:91
msgid ""
"The fastest way to try Mattermost is using the official Docker preview "
"container. This method requires minimal setup and provides a fully "
"functional Mattermost instance."
msgstr ""

